🍋 The average person pees about 6 to 8 times per day.
🚽 Urine is typically 95% water and 5% waste products.
🧃 The yellow color comes from a pigment called urochrome.
🌊 A healthy bladder can hold about 1.5 to 2 cups of urine.
💧 Clear urine might mean you're overhydrated.
🥤 Asparagus can make your pee smell weird — it's totally normal!
🔬 Ancient doctors used to taste pee to diagnose illnesses (yikes).
🦌 Deer and other animals use pee to mark territory.
💥 Holding pee too long can actually weaken your bladder muscles.
🎨 In ancient Rome, urine was used for bleaching clothes.
🧪 Scientists can detect drug use or disease markers from a urine test.
🚫 Foamy pee can sometimes be a sign of kidney problems.
🌈 Pee can turn different colors depending on what you eat (beets = red!).
🧂 Salty foods can make your pee more concentrated and darker.
🚿 Some jellyfish stings should NOT be treated with pee — it's a myth!
💉 Urea, a waste product in urine, is also used in skin creams.
🧃 Bears and other hibernating animals recycle their own urine internally.
🐶 Dogs can “read” each other’s pee like social messages.
🤢 If your pee smells sweet, it could be a sign of diabetes.
🛑 If your pee burns, go see a doctor — seriously!
